From 369db41b57201cea3364da67ab0b8ebda5b929ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:49:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/17] feat(control-plane): export outbox backlog and publish
 attempt metrics

The outbox dispatcher now runs inside the control plane, so a webhook
outage is visible only as WARNING and ERROR log lines until events go
dead. Export two metrics with bounded labels so operators can alert on
event delivery:

- forgemesh_outbox_events{state}: unpublished events, read at scrape
  time and split into pending (never failed), retrying (failed and
  waiting for the backoff) and dead. Outbox.backlog() reads only the
  pending and dead rows through the status index, so the published
  events kept for the retention period do not slow scrapes down.
- forgemesh_outbox_publish_attempts_total{outcome}: published, failed
  (will be retried) or dead (the last attempt). All three series start
  at zero so that increase() also sees the first failure.

The Dispatcher reports an attempt through a new on_attempt callback
only after its outcome is recorded in the database. An attempt whose
outcome could not be recorded is published again and counted then, so
the published count matches the events marked published.

Label values are fixed enums; event ids, event types and tenants are
not labels. The age of the oldest pending event is left out for now.
